+### `dori inbound mattermost [--loop MIN]`
+Prints `INBOUND <source> <channel> <thread-ref> <post-id> <user> <text>[ files=<id>,...]`, keeping Slack's field order: `source` is `dm`, `channel`, `edit:dm` or `edit:channel`, and `thread-ref` is `mattermost:<channel>:<root>`, the thread to answer in (a top-level post is its own root).
+- only `DORI_MATTERMOST_OWNER_ID`'s posts pass; the Dori's own posts, other people's posts and system messages never do;
+- every channel the Dori belongs to is read, DMs and group DMs included, except the ids or names listed in `DORI_MATTERMOST_IGNORE` (comma-separated, names case-insensitive);
+- each new post gets an `eyes` reaction once its line is out; a failed reaction is a `WARN`, and the message is still delivered;
+- an owner edit arrives as its own `edit` kind with the new text. The Dori's reaction changes a post's update time, so only a moved edit time counts as an edit;
+- the newest change seen and the posts already printed are kept in `<stateDir>/mattermost-inbound.json`; a first run starts from now and replays no history;
+- without `--loop` it is one poll; `--loop 0.25` polls every 15 seconds, which keeps the one-minute answer rule.
+
 ### `dori transcribe <audio-file>`
 Runs `hooks.transcribe` and prints the transcript. A failed or empty transcription is an error, never an empty message.
 
